B.cS5=new A.p("scopeRowId",B.D,'priorun-0801 C1: restrict the lane population to CONTAINS-descendants of this row id (literal id or a $-token resolved via resolveFilterToken, e.g. $rowId / $selected:<table>). FAIL-CLOSED: configured-but-unresolved (token has nothing to resolve to yet, e.g. nothing currently selected) scopes to the EMPTY set, never falls back to the unscoped board \u2014 the anti-leak guarantee a per-project lens depends on. Unset (default) = today\'s unscoped behavior. Shows a "Scoped to: X \u2715" chip when resolved; the \u2715 clears the underlying $selected:<table> selection for token scopes.',B.f,null)
B.cWh=new A.p("scopeOptional",B.V,'priorun-0802: opt-in relaxation of scopeRowId\'s fail-closed default \u2014 DEFAULT FALSE, existing behavior byte-identical (still scopes to empty when configured-but-unresolved; a lens must never leak the whole board just because its scope token has not resolved). Set true ONLY for a user-driven SELECTION-CHIP use (e.g. a global view scoped to "whichever row is currently selected", where unresolved means "nothing selected yet", not "the guard rail leaked"): when true and the token is unresolved, renders the FULL unscoped board with no chip; once the token resolves, behavior is identical to the default \u2014 scoped population + the "Scoped to: X \u2715" chip.',B.f,null)
B.d6q=new A.p("limit",B.ag,"dispusab-0804: opt-in TOP-N cap PER LANE \u2014 after scope, filters, sort and lane assignment, each lane renders at most N cards. The PREVIEW idiom: a compact lanes strip on an overview screen beside a button that opens the full Priorities view. Per-lane rather than global, because a global cap would silently empty the later lanes. Unset / <= 0 renders every card (byte-identical to before).",B.f,null)
