B.d0U=new A.p("scopeTargets",B.X,"Restrict the explorer to these subtree root ids (scope the directory to a branch instead of the whole table).",B.f,null)
B.d68=new A.p("nestedScopeTargets",B.X,'A SECOND level of `scopeTargets`-shaped nesting for a `scopeTargets` entry whose own child rows are never a second `explorer` screen \u2014 a JSON object keyed by one of `scopeTargets`\' own tables, each value the SAME `[{table, column}]` list shape as `scopeTargets` itself, e.g. `{"screens": [{"table":"widgets","column":"screen"}, {"table":"pins","column":"screen"}]}`. The normal case (docs/notes/ bublie) needs nothing here: a `scopeTargets` child that IS its own `explorer` screen already gets this discovered for free by walking that screen\'s own `scopeTargets`/`scopeColumn`. This key exists for a scope-target whose children live inside one custom canvas node instead (composer: a board\'s `screens` row owns `widgets`/`pins`/ `frameImages` rows entirely inside the `compose` node, never a second Explorer) \u2014 the host\'s library-shape discovery (e.g. isan\'s `discoverLibraryShape`) reads this key explicitly so file export/ import can still capture those rows. Purely additive/opt-in \u2014 absent for every explorer that predates this key.',B.f,null)
